jobs.description:
Wolfram Chain is looking for a motivated Class C truck driver for a transport company that supplies catering and hospitality businesses, based in Berkel en Rodenrijs.You will work closely with a direct colleague, get to know many regular customers, and at the end of the day, you can enjoy a hot meal at the office for a small fee.Ready for a new challenge? Check out this vacancy or get in touch with us!

Functieomschrijving:
What you will do:As a Class C truck driver for this company, your working days will be focused on supplying hospitality businesses. Your responsibilities include:
• Representing the company and having a friendly conversation with customers;
• Working from Monday to Friday;
• You will deliver food and drinks;
• Want to work extra hours? That's possible. Prefer to work four days a week? That's possible too.

Functievereisten:
What we expect from you as a driver:
• You have a valid Class C or CE driving licence;
• You are physically fit and comfortable performing physically demanding tasks;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English.

Arbeidsvoorwaarden:
What you can expect in return:
• A gross monthly salary between €3,000 and €5,000;
• Overtime paid at 130%, plus an ADV allowance;
• A good pension scheme in accordance with the collective labour agreement (CAO);
• 24 paid vacation days;
• The opportunity to follow internal training courses;
• Getting your class CE license for free;
• A fresh, hot meal every day at the office for just €2.50;
• A permanent contract upon good performance.
Interested?Apply now!

Functie-eisen:
What we expect from you as a driver:
• You have a valid Class C or CE driving licence;
• You are physically fit and comfortable performing physically demanding tasks;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English.

As a Control Panel Builder, you will assemble and wire electrical control panels according to technical drawings and electrical schematics. You make sure that each panel is completed safely, accurately, and in line with the customer’s requirements.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Assembling control cabinets and operator panels;
- Mounting and wiring electrical components;
- Reading and working from electrical drawings and schematics;
- Checking and testing completed control panels;
- Occasionally supporting installation or service work at customer locations.

Most of your work will take place in the workshop, where you will work alongside a team of experienced technicians.

- Technical MBO diploma in Electrical Engineering or related field;
- Experience with control panel assembly is a plus;
- Ability to work from technical and electrical drawings;
- Detail-oriented and quality-focused mindset;
- Able to work independently and in a team;
- English communication skills required.

Vacaturebeschrijving
   Are you looking for a stable job with fixed working hours and a reliable employer? Do you enjoy physical work and working together with colleagues? Then we have a great opportunity for you!
FunctieomschrijvingFor our client, we are looking for motivated Order Pickers to join a modern logistics team. Experience is welcome, but if you are motivated and willing to learn, we would also like to meet you.
As an Order Picker, you play an important role in the warehouse. Every day you make sure customer orders are picked correctly and prepared for delivery. Accuracy is important because customers depend on receiving the right products.
Your daily tasks include:
- Picking orders using a handheld scanner;
- Checking products for quality and quantity;
- Packing and preparing orders for shipment;
- Making sure labels and orders are correct;
- Keeping your workplace clean, safe, and organised;
- Working together with your team to meet daily targets.

The work is active, so you'll be on your feet for most of the day. If you enjoy staying busy instead of sitting behind a desk, this job is a great fit.
Functie-eisenWe are looking for someone who:
- Speaks English, Polish and/or Dutch;
- Works accurately and pays attention to detail;
- Enjoys physical work;
- Can work independently as well as in a team;
- Is willing to work in a chilled warehouse environment;
- Is available to work Monday through Saturday. Working on Sundays and public holidays may also be part of the schedule;
- Has experience with order picking or a handheld scanner (preferred, but not required).

Arbeidsvoorwaarden- A starting salary of €2,600 gross per month (based on full-time employment);
- Shift allowance where applicable;
- Travel allowance;
- A good pension scheme;
- Stable working hours;
- A pleasant and international working environment;
- A reliable employer with long-term opportunities;
- The chance to develop yourself and grow within the company.

Bedrijfsomschrijving

Are you someone who enjoys getting things done and likes working in a modern, well-organized environment? For our client in Montfoort, we are looking for a Warehouse Operative/Orderpicker who will help keep the warehouse running smoothly. You will play an important role in receiving, storing, and shipping goods. This is a full-time position in a fixed shift within a team-oriented environment where collaboration is key and where you will have plenty of opportunities to grow and develop your skills.

As a Warehouse Operative, you play a vital role in the warehouse operation. You ensure that goods are stored in the correct locations, orders are processed on time, and shipments are prepared accurately. You work with attention to detail, think ahead, and maintain an overview in a fast-paced environment. Together with your colleagues, you help ensure that customers can rely on fast and dependable deliveries.

Your responsibilities include:

- Picking orders using handheld scanners and the Warehouse Management System (WMS);
- Checking incoming goods for quantity and quality;
- Moving and storing goods in the correct warehouse locations;
- Preparing orders for shipment, including labeling, packing, and final inspections;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Recording the movement of goods in the system;
- Identifying discrepancies and contributing ideas for process improvements;
- Supporting colleagues with various warehouse tasks.

You will work 40 hours per week and can choose between two shifts:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM
- Evening shift: 04:00 PM – 01:00 AM

You will remain in the same shift at all times, allowing you to maintain a consistent work schedule and routine.

For this position, we are looking for someone who:

- Has an MBO level of education and thinking ability (vocational education level);
- Is proactive, accurate, and detail-oriented;
- Speaks Dutch or English;
- Has their own transportation and can reliably arrive at the workplace on time.
